                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is old, and you can definitely feel it in some parts, but it still holds up pretty well today.\n\nApril is a lovable main character. She's sarcastic and funny without being annoying, and the story and lore are fantastic. The worldbuilding is one of the best parts of the game, and it kept me interested until the end.\n\nSome puzzles feel a bit dated, but nothing too frustrating. My only real disappointment is the ending, which feels a bit anticlimactic after such a great journey. I was hoping for something a little more satisfying.\n\nOverall, it's still a really good game even by today's standards, and an easy recommendation for anyone who enjoys story-driven adventure games. Looking forward to Dreamfall next.",
